Hello [PERSON_1],

Following our call, the points from quality and IT.

Quality
- The cold room and the packing area must be temperature-mapped before go-live, and the
  system must record the temperature every five minutes and alarm when it leaves 2-8 degrees.
- Full audit trail of every user action, kept for five years, with electronic signatures
  for any release of quarantined stock.
- The temperature mapping study itself will be done by our own validation contractor.

IT
- Integration with SAP S/4HANA: order release, goods receipt and stock reconciliation once
  an hour. We are open to IDocs or APIs; our SAP team has not chosen yet.
- The system must be hosted in our own data centre. No public cloud for GDP data.
- Users sign in with our corporate directory; we have not decided whether to use the
  existing on-premises domain or the new cloud tenant.

Volumes
- Today: 2,800 order lines per hour at the morning peak. The hospital tender may add
  between 10% and 40%; we will only know in February.

